course: dictionary
lesson: 10809
title: Vas: a piece of a word, and a French word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Vas» is a strange little word. In English it is hardly ever a word on its own. It is usually a piece of a longer word, like canvas or vascular. In medicine, a vas is a tube in the body that carries fluid.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Tu vas où ?» is French for «Where are you going?» Here vas comes from the French verb aller, which means to go. So tu vas means you go or you are going.
explain: First ask: is this a whole word, or a piece of one? Check the letters before and after it. In vascular, the rest of the word tells you it is about blood vessels. When you know which language you are reading, the meaning becomes clearer.
fact: Vas is a noun in medicine. Its plural is vasa, and it is rare.
fact: Vas deferens is the tube in a man's body that carries sperm.
fact: Vas is a piece of longer words, such as vascular (to do with blood vessels) and canvas.
fact: In French, «Tu vas bien ?» means «Are you well?» and «Vas-y» means «Go on!»
fact: «Yak vas zvut?» is the polite way to ask someone's name, but children rarely ask grown-ups this.
exercise: In «Tu vas où ?», what is vas a form of? | A piece of canvas | The English word vast | A tube in the body | *The French verb aller, to go
exercise: Which word has vas as a piece, and is about blood vessels? | *vascular | breakfast | hiking | sunshine
exercise: A child asks «yak vas zvut?» What is the question? | *What is your name? | How old are you? | Where do you live? | Are you hungry?
test: What is the plural of vas in medicine? | vasi | vases | *vasa | vas
test: Archie says «Salut, tu vas bien ?» to his French teacher. Why does it sound cheeky? | Because she is a child | Because it means goodbye | *Because it is as cheeky as calling her "mate" | Because it is too quiet
exam: What does «Vas-y» mean? | *Go on! | It is a tube in the body | Stop right now | Hello, how are you?
